## Quality gate

Before approving the tasks phase, run `/sdd:spec-lint <feature>` — it verifies every requirement
is covered by a task and every task reference points to a real requirement ID.

Correctness is a separate question from structure: when the work changes a **metric definition, a
canonical dataset, or the agent's domain instructions**, run `/sdd:spec-evals <feature>` and keep the
suite green. Ground truth is authored by a human, never by the agent under test.
This project requires evals for: **{{EVAL_SCOPE}}**.
<!-- e.g. "any change to gold tables or metric definitions" — or "nothing yet; opt-in" -->


## Quick reference

| Command | Use |
|---|---|
| `/sdd:steering` | (re)generate project memory from the codebase |
| `/sdd:absorb-knowledge` | harvest conventions from prior AI configs into steering |
| `/sdd:discover-tools` | map available tools (Jira/git/data) → `integrations.md` |
| `/sdd:spec-init` → `spec-requirements` → `spec-design` → `spec-tasks` → `spec-impl` | the full flow |
| `/sdd:spec-quick "desc" [--spec-only] [--auto]` | run the phases in one command |
| `/sdd:spec-impl-auto <feature> [tasks]` | alias — the same risk-gated loop `spec-impl*` already runs when `autoapprove.json` is enabled |
| `python tools/write-guard.py --self-test` | prove the write-scope hook denies/allows what you think it does |
| `/sdd:spec-lint <feature>` | validate traceability (`--require-evals` to also demand an eval suite) |
| `/sdd:spec-evals <feature> [--run]` | golden questions + regression assertions; measure correctness |
| `/sdd:spec-status <feature>` | progress report |
| `/prepare-pr [base]` | self-review the diff + open a PR on the detected host |
| `/review [<pr>\|--diff]` | review an open PR or your working diff |
| `/data-quality <table> [--spec <feat>]` | run read-only DQ checks on the data platform |
